# Shell scripts must check out with LF on every platform.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text
# files to CRLF in the working copy. For Go sources that is harmless -- the
# compiler does not care, and only `gofmt -l` notices. For a shell script it is
# fatal in a way that is hard to read: a CRLF `#!/usr/bin/env bash` line makes
# the kernel look for an interpreter named "bash\r", and the Linux runner fails
# with `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env: no such file or directory` -- naming env,
# which exists, rather than the carriage return, which is the problem.
#
# The blob is already stored with LF, so this changes nothing on the runner
# today. It is here so that a checkout on a machine configured differently, or a
# script added by someone who is not on Windows, cannot reintroduce it.
*.sh text eol=lf
